It shall be unlawful for a pawnbroker, pawnshop, secondhand dealer, dealer in precious metals and gems or person operating under a license granted pursuant to this article to commit any of the following acts:
(1) Fail to make an entry of any material matter in the daily record of said business;
(2) Make any false entity in the daily record of said business;
(3) Falsify, obliterate or destroy the daily record of said business or remove the daily record from the place of business;
(4) Refuse to allow the county sheriff's department, the city police department or any other duly authorized law enforcement officer to inspect the daily record of said business or any goods in the possession of said business during the ordinary hours of business or at any reasonable time;
(5) Fail to comply with this article in any other material way.
(Ord. of 1-5-2016, § 1(1-11))
